The correct answer is __**Ctrl + S**__.

 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/36f36cd5ece4186095afcf2ffbfb7b80cc04b6c2e3226e7477a419a9fbc96f85.png] **__Key Points__**

__

• **Ctrl + S** is a keyboard shortcut used to save a document in MS Word 2019, not to manipulate the formatting of selected text.

• In MS Word 2019, common keyboard shortcuts for formatting text include:


• **Ctrl + B** - Bold the selected text.

• **Ctrl + I** - Italicize the selected text.

• **Ctrl + U** - Underline the selected text.



• Using **Ctrl + S** ensures that any changes made to the document are saved, preventing data loss.

 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/f13e2ad6582c16aa62a83672e2547ad20a01fddb61962a1acce42eb9a1a99caa.png] **Additional Information__**


• Other useful keyboard shortcuts in MS Word 2019 include:


• **Ctrl + C** - Copy selected text or object.

• **Ctrl + V** - Paste copied text or object.

• **Ctrl + X** - Cut selected text or object.

• **Ctrl + P** - Open the print dialog box.

• **Ctrl + Z** - Undo the last action.



• Knowing and using keyboard shortcuts can significantly improve productivity and efficiency while working with documents.

• Keyboard shortcuts are consistent across many versions of MS Word, making it easier to adapt to newer versions.

